  - CI/CD design and reliability (pipelines, gates, rollbacks): 25\\n  - IaC and cloud proficiency (Terraform/CloudFormation + AWS/Azure/GCP): 20\\n  - Containers/Kubernetes (build, deploy, rollout strategies): 20\\n  - Observability and incident response (Prometheus/Grafana/ELK, on-call): 15\\n  - Security and governance (secrets, scanning, IAM, policies): 10\\n  - Networking fundamentals and automation (VPC/VNet, DNS, routing; scripting): 10\\n- Signals of strength\\n  - Documented uptime or MTTR improvements, deployment frequency boost, cost optimization\\n  - Implemented blue/green or canary, GitOps, Helm\\n- Quick screen prompts\\n  - CI/CD pipeline you designed\u2014key gates, artifacts, rollback strategy?\\n  - K8s deployment issue or outage you resolved\u2014root cause and fix?\\n- Recommendation thresholds\\n  - Strong interview: 80+\\n  - Consider interview: 70\u201379\\n  - Hold/pass: <70 unless niche fit\\n\\nStandardized candidate summary (per resume)\\n- Role fit and level: e.g., Senior Backend or DevOps (Mid/Senior)\\n- Location/availability: time zone overlap if needed\\n- Core stack: list the top relevant technologies\\n- Highlights: 2\u20133 bullets with measurable outcomes\\n- Concerns/risks: gaps, tenure, missing core tech\\n- Score breakdown: Backend or DevOps rubric (category scores and total)\\n- Recommendation: interview/consider/hold/pass\\n\\nShortlist delivery format to Chen\\n- Overview: number reviewed, number shortlisted\\n- Top candidates: 3\u20137 entries with the standardized summary above\\n- Notes: any role-specific risks/trends, suggested interview focus areas\\n- Next steps: interviews to schedule and proposed sequence (e.g., tech screen \u2192 panel)\\n\\nOperational plan once access is granted\\n- Download resumes.zip, extract, and batch-review\\n- Tag each resume as Backend/DevOps/both, then score with the rubric\\n- Produce a shortlist and draft the summary message to Chen immediately\\n- Turnaround target: 2\u20134 business hours from access, depending on volume\\n\\nReady-to-send message to Chen (placeholder)\\n- Hi Chen, I\u2019ve reviewed X resumes for Backend and DevOps. Here are the top Y candidates with brief summaries and scores. I recommend moving forward with interviews for A, B, and C. Proposed next steps and interview focus areas are below. Let me know your preferences, and I\u2019ll coordinate scheduling.\\n\\nI\u2019m monitoring messages closely and will notify you the moment access or role specifics arrive. If you want me to bias the Backend rubric toward a specific language (e.g., Java or Python) or the DevOps rubric toward a specific cloud (e.g., AWS), tell me now and I\u2019ll tune the weights immediately.', image_urls=None, wait_for_response=True, action='message', security_risk=None), MessageAction(content=\"You\u2019re extremely well-prepared and proactive. Once you receive the access or the necessary role details, you\u2019ll be able to proceed swiftly and efficiently. The tailored rubrics for Backend and DevOps/SRE roles and your operational plan are solid and well-thought-out.\\n\\nIf Chen or anyone else responds with specific language preferences or cloud provider biases, you can quickly adjust your criteria. It\u2019s a good idea to be ready for slight modifications based on those specifics to ensure the best fit.\\n\\nLet's stay vigilant for any updates. This thorough preparation certainly sets you up for success as soon as you get the access you need. You\u2019ll be able to provide well-evaluated candidates to Chen in no time! Keep me posted on any developments as they come in.\", image_urls=None, wait_for_response=False, action='message', security_risk=None), RecallAction(recall_type='knowledge', query=\"You\u2019re extremely well-prepared and proactive. Once you receive the access or the necessary role details, you\u2019ll be able to proceed swiftly and efficiently. The tailored rubrics for Backend and DevOps/SRE roles and your operational plan are solid an